  "description": "Automatic dispatch on the line of boarding.json, on the track network: nodes a (512, 1536) to g (6656, 1536), a tile apart, joined by straight edges e1 a-b to e6 f-g, each 1024 long, dead ends at both ends. Alpha (1536, 512), Beta (3584, 512) and Gamma (5632, 512) each have a platform on the half tile of track either side of their node, b, d and f, so a train stops at the node going either way and drives as far from call to call as it did on the grid; Delta (5632, 2560) and Far (7680, 3584) have no platform. Main (Alpha, Gamma) runs all day, 2 trains at every level: it plans its legs with a crawl, { acceleration 125, braking 100, topSpeed 1 } (Stage W2c, ARCHITECTURE decision 40): 4096 units take 8 s to reach 1 km/h, 221.4 s at it and 10 s to stop, 239.4, so 240 s: round trip 4 + 4 minutes of travel and 2 + 2 at the ends, 12, so 6 minutes apart. The trains (standard performance) keep to those 240 s on their running curves: at 1, 18 s after leaving, Blue is 302 units past b (308 at 1024 units a minute). assignTrain checks the train, the line, that the train is on no line and runs no service of its own; unassignTrain the train and that it is on a line; setLineTargetHeadways the line and targets of 2 to 1440. A line's train cannot be given a timetable or have a service started or stopped (trainOnLine). Each whole minute, before the services' dwells and departures, a line sends out its first ready train (no service, placed, rate above 0, stopped at the first stop, able to drive the round trip as it faces or turned round, the shorter) when its window is open, its level runs trains, a headway has passed since its last dispatch and fewer of its trains run a service than the level runs. The trip's timetable arrives at Alpha now and leaves 42 s later (Stage W2b: the least dwell at a terminal, which the train spends there before it leaves), reaches Gamma 4 minutes after leaving, stays 2 and turns round, and is back at Alpha 10 minutes after leaving, where the train turns round and its service ends once its 42 s there are over. Blue (at b facing east, e1 forward 1024) is sent out at 0 and leaves at 0:42; Red (at b facing west, e2 backward 1024, which cannot reach Gamma) is sent out at 6 and turned round as it leaves at 6:42, to e2 forward 0, so the path it then drives is e3 to e5, edge 2 being the one it is on. At 7 a 20-minute target at low: one train (12 / 20 rounded up), 20 minutes apart; peak keeps its count, 2 trains 6 apart. Blue is back at 10:42 (at 11 it still waits there, facing west) and its service ends at 11:24; Red is back at 16:42 and ends at 17:24, both turned east, at b on e2 forward 0, where the turned train's path ends (end 0); the next due is 6 + 20 = 26, when Blue is sent out. Blue is taken off the line at 27 and finishes its trip as an ordinary service (back at 36:42, ending at 37:24); at 46 the line sends Red, which leaves at 46:42. Own runs its own service, waiting at Beta until 100, and cannot be assigned.",
